{"qid": "gf-11", "paper_id": "2001.06899", "answer": true, "unanimous": false, "quote": "The algorithm used in the analysis, the combined secondary vertex (Version 2), is described in Ref. [ 42 ] .", "all_quotes": ["experimental precision is improved with respect to previous LHC results because of the increased size of the data sample and advanced heavy-flavor tagging techniques.", "The algorithm used in the analysis, the combined secondary vertex (Version 2), is described in Ref. [ 42 ] .", "The analysis uses a 'medium' operating point, which corresponds to approximately 10 (60)% tagging efficiencies for $\\mathup{{{c}}}$ ( $\\mathup{{{b}}}$ ) quark jets and a misidentification probability of 1% for a light jet.", "The analysis uses a 'medium' operating point, which corresponds to approximately 10 (60)% tagging efficiencies for $\\mathup{{{c}}}$ ($\\mathup{{{b}}}$ ) quark jets and a misidentification probability of 1% for a light jet.", "SV is reconstructed using an adaptive vertex reconstruction algorithm [ 43 ] from selected tracks within a cone of $\\Delta R<0.3$ around the jet axis.", "In the jet $p_{\\mathrm{T}}$ range between 30 and 200  GeV the efficiencies vary only slightly and range from 8.3 to 11.3% for ${\\mathup{{{Z}}}}\\hskip-2.5pt+\\hskip-1.49994pt{\\mathup{{{c}}}}\\text{~jets}$ and from 45.9 to 60.7% for ${\\mathup{{{Z}}}}\\hskip-2.5pt+\\hskip-1.49994pt{\\mathup{{{b}}}}\\text{~jets}$ events. The ${\\mathup{{{Z}}}}\\hskip-2.5pt+\\hskip-1.49994pt\\text{light~jets}$ mistagging rate increases from 0.3 to 1.0% in the same $p_{\\mathrm{T}}$ range.", "The SV is reconstructed using an adaptive vertex reconstruction algorithm [ 43 ] from selected tracks within a cone of ΔR<0.3 around the jet axis.", "In the jet p_{mathrm{T}} range between 30 and 200  GeV the efficiencies vary only slightly and range from 8.3 to 11.3% for Z+c jets and from 45.9 to 60.7% for Z+b jets events. The Z+light jets mistagging rate increases from 0.3 to 1.0% in the same p_{mathrm{T}} range.", "In the jet $p_{\\mathrm{T}}$ range between 30 and 200  GeV the efficiencies vary only slightly and range from 8.3 to 11.3% for ${\\mathup{{{Z}}}}\\hskip-2.5pt+\\hskip-1.49994pt{\\mathup{{{c}}}~jets}$ and from 45.9 to 60.7% for ${\\mathup{{{Z}}}}\\hskip-2.5pt+\\hskip-1.49994pt{\\mathup{{{b}}}~jets}$ events. The ${\\mathup{{{Z}}}}\\hskip-2.5pt+\\hskip-1.49994pt{light~jets}$ mistagging rate increases from 0.3 to 1.0% in the same $p_{\\mathrm{T}}$ range.", "The $\\mathup{{{c}}}$ and $\\mathup{{{b}}}$ jet identification is performed with the following procedure. To reduce the combinatorics the best pair (triplet) of jets is chosen by minimizing the reconstructed and nominal mass of the $\\mathup{{{W}}}$ boson (top quark). From this optimization, the $\\mathup{{{c}}}$ and $\\mathup{{{b}}}$ jet candidates from top quark and $\\mathup{{{W}}}$ boson decays are identified. The event is kept if these candidates pass the jet HF tagging requirement described in Section 4 .", "In the resulting sample of the $\\mathup{{{c}}}$ jet candidates about half have correct flavor assignment whereas the other half constitute mostly $\\mathup{{{b}}}$ jets that are misidentified as $\\mathup{{{c}}}$ jets.", "The $M_{\text{SV}}$ template for $\\mathup{{{b}}}$ jets is derived from a high-purity data sample of $\\mathup{{{t}}}$ $\\mathup{{\\overline{{{\\mathup{{{t}}}}}}}}$ events decaying to final states of ${\\mathup{{{e}}}}{\\mathup{}}$ $+\\geq$ 2 jets with at least one b-tagged jet.", "Good agreement between the data-driven template shape and the simulation is observed.", "The $\\mathup{{{c}}}$ and $\\mathup{{{b}}}$ jet identification is performed with the following procedure...", "The HF tagging efficiencies for $\\mathup{{{c}}}$ and $\\mathup{{{b}}}$ jets are estimated in simulation and corrected by the efficiency scale factors as described in Section 5.2 . The systematic uncertainties of the efficiency scale factors of $\\mathup{{{c}}}$ jets and $\\mathup{{{b}}}$ jets with $30<p_{\\mathrm{T}}<100\\,\\text{Ge\\hskip-0.80002ptV}$ and $\\lvert\\eta\\rvert<2.4$ are ${\\approx}3.5\\%$ and ${\\approx}1.4\\%$ , respectively [ 42 ] ."], "answers": ["The paper states that the b-tagging efficiency scale factors have a systematic uncertainty of ≈1.4% for b jets in the specified kinematic range, but does not name the algorithm or working point.", "The paper uses an 'adaptive vertex reconstruction algorithm' for SV tagging. The tagging efficiencies are 8.3–11.3% for c jets and 45.9–60.7% for b jets, with a light-jet mistag rate of 0.3–1.0%. No specific b-tagging working point is mentioned.", "The paper uses an adaptive vertex reconstruction algorithm (referenced as [43]) for SV tagging. The tagging efficiencies for c jets range from 8.3% to 11.3%, and for b jets from 45.9% to 60.7% in the jet $p_{\\mathrm{T}}$ range of 30-200 GeV. The mistagging rate for light jets increases from 0.3% to 1.0% in the same range. No specific b-tagging working point is mentioned.", "The paper uses an adaptive vertex reconstruction algorithm for tagging. The b-jet tagging efficiency ranges from 45.9% to 60.7%, while the light-jet mistag rate ranges from 0.3% to 1.0% in the jet $p_{\\mathrm{T}}$ range of 30–200 GeV. The working point is not explicitly stated.", "The paper uses the combined secondary vertex (Version 2) algorithm with a 'medium' working point. It has 10% tagging efficiency for c-jets, 60% for b-jets, and a 1% misidentification probability for light jets.", "The paper uses the combined secondary vertex (Version 2) algorithm with a 'medium' working point. This provides 10% tagging efficiency for c-jets, 60% for b-jets, and a 1% misidentification probability for light jets.", "The paper uses the combined secondary vertex (Version 2) algorithm with the 'medium' working point. This provides 10% tagging efficiency for c-jets, 60% for b-jets, and a 1% misidentification probability for light jets.", "The text refers to an unspecified 'HF tagging requirement' for b/c jet identification. Validation shows ~50% of c-jet candidates are correctly identified, with the rest mostly misidentified b-jets. b-jets are selected using a top-antitop sample requiring at least one b-tagged jet. No explicit algorithm name or working point is provided."], "votes": {"False": 22, "True": 8}, "escalated": false, "sections_read": [" + Abstract + Introduction + The CMS detector + Data and simulated samples", "Appendix B Measured differential cross section ratios", "Cross section ratio measurements + Analysis strategy + $\\mathup{{{Z}}}$ +HF jets event tagging efficiency", "Estimation of the event yields", "Object reconstruction and event selection", "Results + Summary + Appendix A Post-fit $M_{\\text{SV}}$ distributions in the exclusive jet $p_{\\mathrm{T}}$ bins", "Systematic uncertainties", "Unfolding"], "verdicts": [{"paper_id": "2001.06899", "qid": "gf-11", "answer": false, "quote": "", "quote_verified": false, "quotes": [], "reasoning": "", "answer_text": "No information on the b-tagging algorithm, working point, or performance is provided in the given text.", "section": " + Abstract + Introduction + The CMS detector + Data and simulated samples", "window": 0, "escalated": false, "raw": "{\"reasoning\": \"The text does not mention any b-tagging algorithm, working point, or performance metrics related to it. The sections provided discuss the experimental setup, data samples, and simulation details but do not specify the methods used for identifying b-jets.\", \"quotes\": [], \"answer\": \"No information on the b-tagging algorithm, working point, or performance is provided in the given text.\", \"found\": false}"}, {"paper_id": "2001.06899", "qid": "gf-11", "answer": false, "quote": "", "quote_verified": false, "quotes": [], "reasoning": "", "answer_text": "", "section": " + Abstract + Introduction + The CMS detector + Data and simulated samples", "window": 0, "escalated": false, "raw": "{\"reasoning\": \"The text does not mention any specific b-tagg