{"qid": "gf-10", "paper_id": "2001.06899", "answer": true, "unanimous": true, "quote": "Its magnitude, $p_{\\mathrm{T}}^{\\text{miss}}$ , is required to be less than 40  GeV , which results in a signal efficiency of ${\\approx}80\\%$ with the $\\mathup{{{t}}}$ $\\mathup{{\\overline{{{{\\mathup{{{t}}}}}}}}}$ rejection factor of ${\\approx}4.8$ .", "all_quotes": ["Its magnitude, $p_{\\mathrm{T}}^{\\text{miss}}$ , is required to be less than 40  GeV , which results in a signal efficiency of ${\\approx}80\\%$ with the $\\mathup{{{t}}}$ $\\mathup{{\\overline{{{{\\mathup{{{t}}}}}}}}}$ rejection factor of ${\\approx}4.8$ .", "its magnitude, p_{\\mathrm{T}}^{\\text{miss}} , is required to be less than 40  GeV , which results in a signal efficiency of ${\\approx}80\\%$ with the $\\mathup{{{t}}}$ $\\mathup{{\\overline{{{\\mathup{{{t}}}}}}}}$ rejection factor of ${\\approx}4.8$ .", "Its magnitude, p_{\\mathrm{T}}^{\\text{miss}} , is required to be less than 40  GeV , which results in a signal efficiency of ${\\approx}80\\%$ with the $\\mathup{{{t}}}$ $\\mathup{{\\overline{{{{\\mathup{{{t}}}}}}}}}$ rejection factor of ${\\approx}4.8$ .", "In the above formulas, the integrated luminosity as well as the efficiencies that are related to lepton and p_{\\mathrm{T}}^{\\text{miss}} requirements in the {\\mathup{{{Z}}}\\hskip-2.5pt+\\hskip-1.49994pt\\text{jets}} event selection cancel.", "In the above formulas, the integrated luminosity as well as the efficiencies that are related to lepton and p_{\\mathrm{T}}^{\\text{miss}} requirements in the {\\mathup{{{Z}}}}\\hskip-2.5pt+\\hskip-1.49994pt\\text{jets} event selection cancel.", "Missing transverse momentum selection efficiency: This uncertainty source accounts for possible differences in the $p_{\\mathrm{T}}^{\\text{miss}}$ selection ($p_{\\mathrm{T}}^{\\text{miss}}<40\\,\\text{Ge\\hskip-0.80002ptV}$) efficiencies for ${\\mathup{{{Z}}}}\\hskip-2.5pt+\\hskip-1.49994pt\\text{jets}$ and ${\\mathup{{{Z}}}}\\hskip-2.5pt+\\hskip-1.49994pt\\text{HF~jets}$ events. The effect comes from contributions of semileptonic decays of HF hadrons in ${\\mathup{{{Z}}}}\\hskip-2.5pt+\\hskip-1.49994pt\\text{HF~jets}$ events, which results in large $p_{\\mathrm{T}}^{\\text{miss}}$ values. Therefore, the efficiencies tend to be lower for ${\\mathup{{{Z}}}}\\hskip-2.5pt+\\hskip-1.49994pt\\text{HF~jets}$ events by ${\\approx}1\\%$ at high jet and $\\mathup{{{Z}}}$ boson $p_{\\mathrm{T}}$ regions compared to those of ${\\mathup{{{Z}}}}\\hskip-2.5pt+\\hskip-1.49994pt\\text{jets}$ events. An uncertainty of 1.5% is included in the R(c/j) and R(b/j) differential results for jet ($\\mathup{{{Z}}}$ boson) $p_{\\mathrm{T}}$ bins where $p_{\\mathrm{T}}>60$ (90)  GeV .", "Missing transverse momentum selection efficiency: This uncertainty source accounts for possible differences in the $p_{\\mathrm{T}}^{\\text{miss}}$ selection ($p_{\\mathrm{T}}^{\\text{miss}}<40\\,\\text{Ge\\hskip-0.80002ptV}$) efficiencies for ${\\mathup{{{Z}}}\\hskip-2.5pt+\\hskip-1.49994pt\\text{jets}}$ and ${\\mathup{{{Z}}}\\hskip-2.5pt+\\hskip-1.49994pt\\text{HF~jets}}$ events. The effect comes from contributions of semileptonic decays of HF hadrons in ${\\mathup{{{Z}}}\\hskip-2.5pt+\\hskip-1.49994pt\\text{HF~jets}}$ events, which results in large $p_{\\mathrm{T}}^{\\text{miss}}$ values. Therefore, the efficiencies tend to be lower for ${\\mathup{{{Z}}}\\hskip-2.5pt+\\hskip-1.49994pt\\text{HF~jets}}$ events by ${\\approx}1\\%$ at high jet and $\\mathup{{{Z}}}$ boson $p_{\\mathrm{T}}$ regions compared to those of ${\\mathup{{{Z}}}\\hskip-2.5pt+\\hskip-1.49994pt\\text{jets}}$ events. An uncertainty of 1.5% is included in the R(c/j) and R(b/j) differential results for jet ($\\mathup{{{Z}}}$ boson) $p_{\\mathrm{T}}$ bins where $p_{\\mathrm{T}}>60$ (90)  GeV ."], "answers": ["The pT^miss < 40 GeV cut retains a signal efficiency of approximately .8 (80%)", "The pT^miss < 40 GeV cut retains a signal efficiency of approximately 80%"], "votes": {"False": 27, "True": 