an SF-OS lepton pair (from Z decay) and an additional lepton (from top quark decay) are present. The SF-OS pair identifies the Z boson decay, while the additional lepton helps distinguish the signal from background.\",\n\"found\": true\n}"}, {"paper_id": "2006.05880", "qid": "gf-06", "answer": true, "quote": "Unlike other top squark models, these signals can be efficiently distinguished from the SM top quark pair production ( $t\\bar{t}$ ) background by requiring either a same-flavour opposite-sign (SF-OS) lepton pair originating from the $Z\\to\\ell^{+}\\ell^{-}$ ( $\\ell\\equiv e,\\mu$ ) decay or a pair of $b$ -tagged jets originating from the $h\\to b\\bar{b}$ decay, plus the presence of an additional lepton produced in the decay of the top quarks in the event.", "quote_verified": true, "quotes": ["Unlike other top squark models, these signals can be efficiently distinguished from the SM top quark pair production ( $t\\bar{t}$ ) background by requiring either a same-flavour opposite-sign (SF-OS) lepton pair originating from the $Z\\to\\ell^{+}\\ell^{-}$ ( $\\ell\\equiv e,\\mu$ ) decay or a pair of $b$ -tagged jets originating from the $h\\to b\\bar{b}$ decay, plus the presence of an additional lepton produced in the decay of the top quarks in the event."], "reasoning": "", "answer_text": "The region requiring at least three leptons uses an SF-OS lepton pair from $Z$ decay and an additional lepton from top quark decay.", "section": " + Introduction", "window": 0, "escalated": false, "raw": "{\"reasoning\": \"The text mentions regions requiring three leptons and their roles in distinguishing signals from background.\", \"quotes\": [\"Unlike other top squark models, these signals can be efficiently distinguished from the SM top quark pair production ( $t\\\\bar{t}$ ) background by requiring either a same-flavour opposite-sign (SF-OS) lepton pair originating from the $Z\\\\to\\\\ell^{+}\\\\ell^{-}$ ( $\\\\ell\\\\equiv e,\\\\mu$ ) decay or a pair of $b$ -tagged jets o